---
import DocShell from '../../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../../lib/nav';

const toc = [
   { id: 'install', label: 'Install the skill' },
   { id: 'first-run', label: 'First run' },
   { id: 'behavior', label: 'What it changes' },
   { id: 'mcp', label: 'Skill and MCP' },
   { id: 'update', label: 'Update' },
];
---

<DocShell
   title="Install the agent skill"
   summary="The skill is a set of instructions that teaches a coding agent how to use a11ied: check coverage before testing, pick the target that matches the question, and keep automated results apart from screen reader transcripts."
   links={docsLinks}
   toc={toc}
>
   <section class="split panel" id="install">
      <div class="stack">
         <div class="panel-head">
            <p class="panel-kicker">Install</p>
            <h2>Install it with aix</h2>
         </div>
         <p>
            <a href="http://aix.a1st.dev/">aix</a> finds the coding agents installed on your machine
            and asks which one gets the skill. Installing at user scope makes it available to that
            agent in every project.
         </p>
         <pre><code>npx -y @a1st/aix install https://github.com/hypothesi/a11ied/blob/master/packages/skills/ai.json --only skills --user</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="split-aside">
         <div class="tag">Skip the prompt</div>
         <p class="aside-note">
            Add <code>--target claude-code</code>, <code>--target codex</code>, or another supported
            target to install without being asked.
         </p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="first-run">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">First run</p>
         <h2>Give the agent a route and a job</h2>
      </div>
      <ol>
         <li>Install the <code>a1</code> command if it is not already on the machine.</li>
         <li>Restart the coding agent so it picks up the new skill.</li>
         <li>Start the app you want to test.</li>
         <li>Name the route and the behavior you want checked.</li>
      </ol>
      <pre><code>npm install --global a11ied

a1 doctor</code></pre>
      <pre data-label="AI AGENT PROMPT"><code>Use the a11ied skill to test http://localhost:3000/checkout.
Run the automated checks first, then test the field labels and the
error messages with the screen reader. Keep the two results separate.</code></pre>
   </section>

   <section class="ledger" id="behavior">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Behavior</p>
         <h2>What the skill changes</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong>Resolves the criterion first</strong>
            <span>When the task is framed in WCAG terms, the agent looks up the criterion and its coverage before it runs anything.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong>Checks applicability</strong>
            <span>The agent inspects the page for relevant signals instead of running all 86 criteria against every route.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong>Picks the evidence mode on purpose</strong>
            <span>Automated when the runtime can decide, hybrid when a person judges part of it, manual when the runtime can only explain the criterion.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong>Escalates from virtual to real</strong>
            <span>The virtual reader for fast local loops, VoiceOver or NVDA when the real software's behavior is the question.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong>Separates evidence from claims</strong>
            <span>Automated results, transcripts, and human judgment stay distinct. A passing axe run is not reported as conformance.</span>
         </div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="split panel" id="mcp">
      <div class="stack">
         <div class="panel-head">
            <p class="panel-kicker">Together</p>
            <h2>Skill and MCP do different jobs</h2>
         </div>
         <p>
            The skill tells the agent how to reason about a test. The MCP server gives it the tools
            to run one. They work independently, and they work better together.
         </p>
         <p>
            Follow <a href="/guides/agents">test from an AI agent</a> to connect MCP. Use the
            <a href="/reference/mcp">MCP reference</a> when you need exact tool inputs.
         </p>
      </div>
      <div class="split-aside">
         <div class="tag">Source</div>
         <p class="aside-note">
            The installed instructions come from <code>packages/skills/a11ied/SKILL.md</code> in the
            repository.
         </p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note" id="update">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Update</p>
         <h2>Run the install command again</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
         The same <code>aix install</code> command pulls the current skill from the repository and
         reinstalls it at user scope.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
